.TH CTI-AGENT-DOCTOR 1 "2026-11-25" "cti-agent" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
cti-agent-doctor \- is this box healthy? one line per check, read-only
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo cti\-agent\-doctor
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the box's health checks and prints one line each,
.BR OK ,
.B WARN
or
.BR FAIL ,
with what to do about anything that is not OK.
.TP
.B version
The installed release
.RI ( /etc/cti\-agent/version )
against the kit it was installed from. A box behind its own kit was pulled
but not reinstalled.
.TP
.B settings
.BR "fleet\-config check" :
missing, misspelt or misplaced settings.
.TP
.B units
Any of the fleet's systemd units in a failed state.
.TP
.B timers
Every timer of a lane this box runs
.RB ( FLEET_LANES )
is enabled. The Patch Tuesday timer is off on purpose and is only noted.
.TP
.B credentials
Today's credential report
.RI ( /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/credcheck.txt ):
every check ok, and written in the last 26 hours.
.TP
.B lane health
Every lane this box runs that has a health report
.RI ( /opt/cti\-agent/share/health.list ,
from the lane manifests) has a current one in
.IR /var/lib/cti\-agent/reports/health/<lane>.json :
present, readable, not an error, and no older than its lane allows. Says how
many gaps are open that nobody declared by design. A WARN, never a FAIL: the
gaps are the check-in's to escalate
.RB ( fleet\-health (1)).
.TP
.B org pack
The org pack the installer uses, when there is one, passes
.BR "org\-pack check \-\-root\-owned" .
It is found the installer's way: a fork's
.I org/
in the kit, or
.I /etc/cti\-agent/org
on a box installed from upstream. Both at once is a FAIL.
.TP
.B beat files
.BR "run\-checkin \-\-audit" :
the orchestrator's files are root-owned and nothing in the service account's
reach could steer a beat.
.PP
It changes nothing and prints no setting's value.
.B cti\-agent\-update
runs it after every update. Root only.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the checks as a JSON list of
.RI { check ", " state ", " detail }.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo cti\-agent\-doctor
sudo cti\-agent\-doctor \-\-json | jq '.[] | select(.state != "OK")'
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when no check FAILs (WARNs included), 1 when one does, 2 for a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cti\-agent\-update (1),
.BR fleet\-config (1),
.BR run\-credcheck (1),
.BR run\-checkin (1)
